accinated (3+Hib) ranged from 50.9% in Rhode Island to 97.7% in New Hampshire.\"}]}], \"study_design\": [{\"v\": \"evaluation or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"CDC used preliminary data from the first half of 2009 NIS to compare the new measures with the previous 3+Hib measure.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"CDC also plans to use the full year of 2009 NIS data to evaluate 1) compliance with interim recommendations\"}]}, {\"v\": \"cross-sectional\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"NIS is a random-digit-dialed telephone survey of households with children aged 19--35 months at the time of interview.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Data were weighted to adjust for households with multiple telephone lines, household nonresponse, and exclusion of households without landline telephones\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The two measures were estimated assuming the Hib vaccines with missing type information were a type requiring 3 doses for the primary series\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"A Hib vaccine reported with an unknown type was assumed to not be a Merck product.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}